  "summary": "Retain combined-axillary-relief-v12 (84d03232-5dbb-4067-8b4a-f849e1d44f31) as an unqualified bilateral shoulder axillary relief and hip deformation diagnostic only. Method v12 inherits bilateral shoulder proximal-arm section handles and dual-plane hip retraction field, and refines the bilateral 60\u00b0 axillary fossa hollow relief to address compound elbow flexion and adduction on both sides: Left arm adds medial +3.5mm dx and anterior +2.5mm dy with -5mm posterior fold centering; Right arm adds medial -3.5mm dx and anterior +3.0mm dy with -15mm posterior fold centering. Result across 25 poses: Pose 15 (UpperArmL-60-child60-twist0) drops to EXACT ZERO contacts (364 baseline -> 20 in v11 -> 0 in v12); Pose 18 (UpperArmR-60-child60-twist0) drops to 14 contacts (414 baseline -> 33 in v11 -> 14 in v12); Pose 16 drops to 48 (from 396 baseline / 56 in v11); Pose 17 drops to 45 (from 443 baseline / 71 in v11). All straight 60\u00b0 shoulders (Left 348->0, Right 390->0), all straight 90\u00b0 shoulders (Left 93->0, Right 166->0), all compound 90\u00b0 shoulders (Left 107->0, Right 178->0), and all three hip poses (10: 42->0, 22: 17->0, 23: 42->0) maintain EXACT ZERO contacts. In total, 22 of 25 evaluated poses achieve EXACT ZERO contacts. Across all 25 evaluated poses, there are ZERO contact regressions, ZERO seam openings, condition number <= 10 (1.172 on shoulders, 1.425 on hips), and all displacements strictly respect frozen caps (hips max posed 0.00819H / cap 0.03H, max rest 0.01159H / cap 0.04H; shoulders max posed 0.01800H / cap 0.02H, max rest 0.01898H / cap 0.02H). Bilateral morph normal delta transport on all four shoulder targets eliminates active support normal divergence on training poses to < 0.000019\u00b0 with 0 support vertices worse over 1\u00b0, passes Khronos gltf-validator with 0 errors, and verifies Babylon GPU shader defines (BONETEXTURE, MORPHTARGETS_NORMAL, NUM_BONE_INFLUENCERS 8, NUM_MORPH_INFLUENCERS 7, NONUNIFORMSCALING absent). All assets remain unqualified diagnostic evidence only.",
